{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשוח בשדה", :translit "la'suach ba'sadeh", :gloss "to meditate/pray in the field"} {:he "על זאת יתפלל כל חסיד אליך לעת מצוא", :translit "al zot yitpalel kol chasid elekha la'et metzo", :gloss "for this shall every godly one pray to You at a time of finding"} {:he "מצא אשה מצא טוב", :translit "matsa ishah matsa tov", :gloss "he found a wife, he found good"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the phrase לעת מצוא is read through מצא אשה מצא טוב so 'a time of finding' means finding a wife"}], :frame {:text "Isaac went out לשוח בשדה (Genesis 24:63), understood as prayer: he established the Minhah prayer (Berakhot 26b, Yerushalmi Berakhot 4:1). The verse לעת מצוא (Psalms 32:6) is read as referring to finding a wife, connecting Isaac's prayer with Rebecca's arrival, since Proverbs 18:22 says מצא אשה מצא טוב.", :sources ["Genesis 24:63" "Psalms 32:6" "Proverbs 18:22" "Berakhot 26b" "Yerushalmi Berakhot 4:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לפנות ערב", :translit "lifnot erev", :gloss "when evening turns"} {:he "והיה לפנות ערב ירחץ במים", :translit "vehayah lifnot erev yirchatz ba'mayim", :gloss "and when evening turns he shall wash in water"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לפנות ערב" "והיה לפנות ערב"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase לפנות ערב occurs twice in Scripture: here (Genesis 24:63) and in Leviticus 15:5 — והיה לפנות ערב ירחץ במים. The latter phrase is the prooftext for the halakhic rule that one who must immerse may do so from the time of Minhah onward (Shabbat 9b). The shared phrase לפנות ערב links both verses to the Minhah time-frame: here Isaac established the Minhah prayer (Berakhot 26b), and there immersion is permitted from Minhah.", :sources ["Genesis 24:63" "Leviticus 15:5" "Shabbat 9b" "Berakhot 26b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the phrase לעת מצוא is read through מצא אשה מצא טוב so 'a time of finding' means finding a wife", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לפנות ערב" "והיה לפנות ערב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לפנות ערב", :refs ["Genesis 24:63" "Deuteronomy 23:12"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והיה לפנות ערב", :refs ["Deuteronomy 23:12"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:57.144860391Z", :model "glm-5.2"}